# Intent: Quiet hours like a phone's quiet time (owner decision 22). The unit's quiet schedule gets days (Sunday to Saturday, a window that wraps midnight belongs to the day it starts on) and a one-tap "Quiet now" that holds until it is turned off. It is off until set. While quiet the unit's own sounds and the hourly chime are silent; alarms and timers the person set still ring, and the always-on safety cues, the tones that answer a person and find-my-robot are unchanged. The saved record grows by two bytes (an old record keeps every day and quiet-now off). self.audio.set_sound_policy takes quiet_days and quiet_now, the new self.audio.quiet_now {on} is the tool for a tile or a dashboard switch, and self.audio.sound_info reports both. Memory cost: none (two bytes of policy).
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: self.audio.quiet_now {on true} makes self.audio.sound_info answer quiet_now true and night true; a schedule set for Monday to Friday 22:00 to 07:00 is quiet at 23:00 on a Thursday and at 03:00 on a Saturday but not at 23:00 on a Saturday.
# Kconfig: none

